  "system": "You are the test generator in Ledger. For one verified business rule of a legacy COBOL batch program you write test fixtures: complete, consistent sets of input records that exercise each branch of the rule and its boundaries. Every case is run through both the original COBOL program and a Python port, and their outputs are compared field by field, so a good case makes the rule's behaviour visible in the output files.\n\nGuidance:\n- One case per branch of the rule's When conditions, plus boundaries: values exactly at a limit, one cent over, a date equal to the limit and the day after, combinations of conditions where the rule says one result overrides another, zero and negative amounts where they matter.\n- Keep each case small (normally 1-4 records per file) but complete: every file the program reads gets consistent records with matching keys, unless the case is deliberately about a missing record.\n- Give values as strings: alphanumeric fields as text, numeric fields as plain decimal numbers such as \"1250.75\" or \"-40.00\" (no sign encoding, no padding). Omitted numeric fields default to 0 and omitted alphanumeric fields to spaces. Use the copybook field names exactly.\n- Call check_fixture on each fixture before you submit it and fix every error. Warnings may be intentional (for example a card that is deliberately missing).\n- Write 3 to 6 cases. In \"expectation\", say what the rule implies should happen; it is a note for reviewers, not the pass/fail oracle.",
  "messages": [
   {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBACT04C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nDISCGRP: CVTRA02Y DIS-GROUP-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID            X(10)\n  DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DIS-INT-RATE                 S9(4)V9(2)\nThe program runs with job PARM '2022071800'. Account, cross-reference and disclosure group files are read by key, so every category balance's account needs ACCOUNT and XREF records.\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBACT04C-002\",\n \"title\": \"The last account group is never written back at end of file\",\n \"summary\": \"The end-of-file branch that should update the last account (ELSE PERFORM 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT) can never run. The loop condition is tested before each pass, so the loop ends as soon as END-OF-FILE becomes 'Y'. The last account in the category balance file therefore never gets its interest added or its cycle credit and debit zeroed, but its interest transactions are still written.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"END-OF-FILE starts as 'N'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The main loop repeats until END-OF-FILE = 'Y', and the test is made before each pass. Inside the loop, the ELSE branch that performs the account update is taken only when END-OF-FILE is not 'N' at the top of a pass.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\",\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"For each category balance record whose DIS-INT-RATE is not zero, 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST is performed inside the loop.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DIS-INT-RATE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST adds the record's monthly interest into WS-TOTAL-INT and right away performs 1300-B-WRITE-TX to produce an interest transaction.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-MONTHLY-INT\",\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The interest transaction record is written to the transaction file at that point, before and separately from any account update.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"FD-TRANFILE-REC\",\n    \"TRAN-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"Reading the category balance file returns status '10' (end of file), which sets APPL-RESULT to 16.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TCATBALF-STATUS\",\n    \"APPL-RESULT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"10\",\n    \"16\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"APPL-EOF (APPL-RESULT value 16) causes END-OF-FILE to be set to 'Y'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"In the same pass, the inner check END-OF-FILE = 'N' is now false, so no more processing is done in that pass.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The loop condition END-OF-FILE = 'Y' is tested before the next pass, so the loop ends without evaluating the outer IF END-OF-FILE = 'N' again.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\",\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"So the outer IF's ELSE branch, which performs 1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT, is never run.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"1050-UPDATE-ACCOUNT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"As a result, the last account group's WS-TOTAL-INT is never added to ACCT-CURR-BAL, its cycle credit and debit are not zeroed, and its account record is not rewritten. If the file is empty, no account is updated at all.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-BAL\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ]\n}"
   }
